              tory locking must still be enabled on a per‐file basis,  as  de‐
              scribed  in  ffccnnttll(2).)   Since Linux 4.5, this mount option re‐
              quires the CCAAPP__SSYYSS__AADDMMIINN capability and a kernel configured with
              the CCOONNFFIIGG__MMAANNDDAATTOORRYY__FFIILLEE__LLOOCCKKIINNGG option.  Mandatory locking has
              been fully deprecated in Linux 5.15, so this flag should be con‐
